v1.0~7:
	on-screen keyboard too large on the official 7" touchscreen, bottom row
	cut off: gui-v2 picks its layout from the physical size Qt reports. The
	panel reports 154 x 86 mm, which gui-v2 rounds to 7 inch and so uses the
	1024x600 layout of the GX Touch 70 on an 800x480 panel. The Qt keyboard
	isn't scaled down with the rest of the UI. /etc/qt-kms.conf now reports
	a 5 inch size for the DSI display, so gui-v2 uses its native 800x480
	layout (GX Touch 50). The DPI isn't affected (eglfs always uses 100 dpi),
	and HDMI displays don't change

v1.0~6:
	RpiDisplaySetup must be uninstalled (package conflict): its settings are
	for the firmware display driver and don't apply under KMS, and it writes
	/etc/venus/backlight_device and blank_display_device for rpi_backlight, a
	backlight that doesn't exist under KMS (the 7" display has 10-0045), so
	dimming and display off failed. Such stale files are now replaced

v1.0~5:
	dimming and display off on the official 7" touchscreen: the raspberrypi2
	firmware has no /etc/venus/backlight_device and blank_display_device, so
	venus-platform had no brightness setting and gui-v2 reported
	"ScreenBlanker: not supported". A udev rule records the display backlight
	in /run/RpiGuiV2 at boot and both files link there. Without a backlight
	(HDMI) nothing changes. Files the firmware provides are left alone

v1.0~4:
	add setup option rotate180: rotates the display 180 degrees through the
	kernel command line (video=<connector>:<mode>,rotate=180 in
	/u-boot/cmdline.txt, repeating the mode the firmware passes) and rotates touch input in qt6.sh to match.
	The firmware rotation settings don't work with KMS

v1.0~3:
	add disable_overscan=1 to the config.txt block: with KMS the firmware
	otherwise passes 48 pixel margins, a black border on HDMI displays.
	An older block is replaced when the package is updated (reboot needed)

v1.0~2:
	fix gui-v2 crashing (SIGBUS, alignment exception) right after start: the
	vc4 driver is rebuilt with a mesa fix that allocates the GL matrix stack
	16-byte aligned (build/patches/0001-mesa-align-the-matrix-stack.patch)

v1.0~1:
	first beta: vc4 KMS overlay, mesa vc4 driver, Qt eglfs configuration,
	display-hotplug fix, gui-v2 from the Victron feed and a start-gui service
	for the Raspberry Pi 2 / 3 / Zero 2 W (machine raspberrypi2)
